k  to his trailer Carrey kicked a hole in  the wall and told director Ron Howard he  couldn't do the movie in an interview on  the Graham Norton Show he had harsh  words for the experience when I did the  Grinch I was literally the makeup was  like being buried alive every day  the first day was eight and a half hours  Carrey was only persuaded to stay when  the production hired someone who trained  CIA operatives to withstand torture to  assist Carrey in dealing with the daily  ordeal the key lesson was in pain  deferment and the actor often punched  himself in the leg if he was having a  particularly hard time Carrey remembers  the hundred days spent in the costume as  a real lesson in Zen it's amazing what  humans can endure in the end it seems  the torture was well worth it The Grinch  earned more than 345 million dollars in  worldwide box office sales making it the  second highest-grossing Christmas movie  of all time Emma Watson landed the role  of Hermione Granger and Harry Potter and  the Sorcerer's Stone at age 9 and  quickly became a fan favorite for her  layered portrayal of the character but  when Watson's contract came up for  renewal as the fifth installment of the  series was being shot rumors swirled  that she was ready to quit the problem  starring in the Harry Potter films  wasn't going to leave Watson time for a  college education had a real fight on my  hands to ensure that I was able to go to  university and I was able to sit my  a-levels the original schedule wouldn't  have left time for Watson to do any of  that and she was willing to quit over  the matter luckily the studio reworked  the shoot to accommodate Watson's  educational aspirations fast-forward to  the happy ending she continued to play  the beloved character in the final films  and earned a degree in English  literature from Brown University  [Music]  plan your carts pathetic we've got final  exams coming up soon Brad Pitt is known  for being an affable charismatic guy but  one loo